---
// Data deletion instructions for AI Ads Lab (Meta app 4704400319834510).
// Meta accepts a "Data Deletion Instructions URL" in place of a callback.
import PolicyLayout from '../../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---
<PolicyLayout
  title="AI Ads Lab Data Deletion"
  description="How to disconnect AI Ads Lab from your Meta account and have HMFIC Marketing LLC delete your data."
  path="/ai-ads-lab/data-deletion"
  updated="October 21, 2026"
>
  <p>
    You can stop AI Ads Lab's access to your Meta account and have all of your
    data deleted at any time. There are two steps: disconnecting the app, then
    asking us to delete what we've stored.
  </p>

  <h2>Step 1: Disconnect AI Ads Lab from Facebook</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Go to <a href="https://www.facebook.com/settings/?tab=business_tools">Facebook Settings → Business Integrations</a>.</li>
    <li>Find <strong>AI Ads Lab</strong> in the list.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Remove</strong> and confirm.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    This immediately stops our access to your Meta ad account, Pages, and
    business portfolio. Campaigns already in your ad account stay there and
    stay under your control. Pause or delete them in Meta Ads Manager if you
    want them to stop.
  </p>

  <h2>Step 2: Ask us to delete your data</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:matt@hmficmarketing.com?subject=AI%20Ads%20Lab%20data%20deletion%20request">matt@hmficmarketing.com</a>
    with the subject line <strong>"AI Ads Lab data deletion request"</strong>,
    from the email address on your AI Ads Lab account.
  </p>
  <p>Within 30 days, we will delete:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your stored Meta access token and the ID of the ad account you connected.</li>
    <li>Campaign and performance data we pulled from your ad account.</li>
    <li>Your onboarding answers, ad plans, copy, scripts, images, and uploaded files.</li>
    <li>Your portal account.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We keep only what the law requires, such as billing records held by Stripe.
    We will email you to confirm when the deletion is done.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
